Usage: expr EXPRESSION

Evaluate expressions.

Print the value of EXPRESSION to standard output.

Supported GNU-style operators and keywords:
  ARG1 | ARG2, ARG1 & ARG2
  ARG1 < ARG2, <=, =, ==, !=, >=, >
  ARG1 + ARG2, ARG1 - ARG2, ARG1 * ARG2, ARG1 / ARG2, ARG1 % ARG2
  STRING : REGEXP, match STRING REGEXP
  substr STRING POS LENGTH, index STRING CHARS, length STRING
  + TOKEN, ( EXPRESSION )

Regex matching uses WinuxCmd's POSIX basic regex module and is anchored at the start of STRING. Numeric arithmetic uses arbitrary-precision integers like GNU expr.

OPTIONS:
                 evaluate expressions
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
